  "behavior_evidence": [
    "Native event rows cover inline growth, inline/heap relocation, copy=false, heap-to-inline reuse after shrink, equal size, ascending destruction, all four move-assignment storage combinations, and inline/heap move construction.",
    "Baseline executable shrink order is [15,14,13,12]; native and candidate are [12,13,14,15].",
    "Move callbacks run for every inline source before any moved-from destructor; heap move transfers the allocation without callbacks. Assignment destroys receiver values before invoking source move callbacks.",
    "Shrinking destroys removed elements in place; explicit address-sensitive destructor tests protect against accidental drain/move destruction.",
    "Rust destructor panic checks prove remaining values are destroyed exactly once under strict Miri. Native noexcept destructor exceptions are outside the common domain."
  ],
